      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>What is a good chest-to-waist ratio?</h3></summary><p>For men, a chest at least 1.2 to 1.3 times the waist gives a visible V shape, and around 1.4 looks muscular. For women, bust and waist are better compared with the hips, which is what body shape calculators do.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>Is shoulder-to-waist ratio the same as the Adonis index?</h3></summary><p>Yes. The Adonis index is a popular name for the shoulder-to-waist ratio, usually with the golden ratio of 1.618 as the target. It is a measure of looks, not of health.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>How can I improve my shoulder-to-waist ratio?</h3></summary><p>Reduce the waist by losing body fat, and build the shoulders and upper back with overhead presses, lateral raises, pull-ups and rows. Losing 2 inches of waist changes the ratio about as much as adding 2.5 inches of shoulder circumference.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>Does shoulder-to-waist ratio matter for women?</h3></summary><p>It matters less. For women, the relationship between bust, waist and hips describes shape better. A shoulder-to-waist ratio well above the average often goes with an inverted triangle or hourglass shape.</p></details>
  </section>

